  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts for the click-to-plant garden. It passes `typecheck`, but I haven't run it in a browser or built it with `vite build`, so none of the behaviour below has been checked. The ground-click mapping is the riskiest part: it assumes the camera's `fov` is vertical and in degrees.\n\n- **Scene:** a 22×22 ground plane sits under a sky-coloured background, seen from a fixed angled camera. It has a hemisphere light and a directional sun with soft PCF shadows.\n- **Plants:** each plant is a stem, four leaves, six petals and a centre. The plants are drawn from four instanced meshes with room for 300 plants. Unused slots are hidden below the ground.\n- **Growth:** a plant grows smoothly over 8 seconds, timed with `performance.now()`. A sprout is a short pale stem with two small leaves. A mature plant is a tall, darker green stem with four leaves and a bloom. The bloom's hue, size and the plant's height vary per plant. A plant planted later is always smaller than an earlier one.\n- **Clicking:** a canvas click is turned into a ray from the camera and intersected with the ground. The plant goes at the hit point. Clicks that miss the ground are ignored, and so are plants beyond 300.\n- **Performance:** the instance buffers are rebuilt only while something is growing or has changed.\n- **Overlay:** a fixed top-left box shows `Plants: N` and a Clear button that removes all plants.\n- **Exposed API:**\n  - `window.__TASK_STATE__` is read-only, with live `plantCount`, `plants` ({x, z, growth}) and `ready`.\n  - `window.__plantAt(x, z)` plants the same way a click does.\n  - `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()`.\n\n",
